nash::diagnostic

  × I am partway through parsing a record type. I just saw a record field, so I was
  │ expecting to see a colon next:
   ╭─[src/Main.nash:1:3]
 1 │ f = value
   ·   ─
   ╰────
  help: Try putting a : followed by a type?

        Note: I may be confused by indentation. For example, if you are trying to define
        a record type across multiple lines, I recommend using this format:

            { name : string
            , age : int
            , value : 'a
            }

        Notice that each line starts with some indentation. Usually two or four spaces.
        This is the stylistic convention in the Nash ecosystem.
